 ## Operating characteristics
-- **Time Complexity:** $O(D_x \cdot D_y \cdot D_z)$, as every input voxel is visited exactly once to compute the sum [S1].
-- **Memory Complexity:** $O(D_x \cdot D_y \cdot D_z)$ for the input and $O(\frac{D_x}{N_x} \cdot \frac{D_y}{N_y} \cdot \frac{D_z}{N_z})$ for the output [S1]. The total memory requirement is dominated by the input and output maps fitting in RAM simultaneously [S1].
-- **Performance:** Performance is limited by memory bandwidth and available RAM; the command may fail for lack of memory [S1].
-- **Strengths:** Simple to implement; deterministic; preserves the mean value of the data in each region [S1].
-- **Limitations:** Loses high-frequency spatial details; truncates data at boundaries if dimensions are not divisible by bin size [S1].
-- **When to use:** When a uniform, fast downsampling is required for level-of-detail generation or memory reduction [S1].
-- **When not to use:** When preserving sharp edges or high-frequency details is critical; when the data distribution requires non-linear binning for visualization (use Iso-Dist instead) [S2, unofficial].
